  "explanation": "We place pointers at both ends of the array. The area is constrained by the shorter line, so at each step we calculate the current container volume and then move the pointer pointing to the shorter height inward, attempting to find a taller boundary.",
  "pseudoCode": "FUNCTION maxArea(height):\n    left = 0, right = LENGTH(height) - 1, maxW = 0\n    WHILE left < right DO:\n        area = (right - left) * MIN(height[left], height[right])\n        maxW = MAX(maxW, area)\n        IF height[left] < height[right] THEN left = left + 1\n        ELSE right = right - 1\n    END WHILE\n    RETURN maxW\nEND FUNCTION",
